 rs the Heritage Monitoring Scouts program\, which the Florida Public Archa
 eology Network started to track changes to cultural sites threatened by se
 a level rise and erosion. The program marks its 10-year anniversary and th
 e talk covers its impact from Pensacola to Tallahassee. The speaker is Kat
 e Schreiber\, the program's coordinator at the network. Light refreshments
  are served and parking at the network's building is free.\n\nPrice: No pu
 blished price\n\nDetails: https://coastaleventures.com/events/ev-pas-herit
